vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: bash]\n[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: task]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: todowrite]\nThe whole suite passes now: `python3 -m unittest` ran 16 tests, all OK. Before, it reported 15; the jump is because `test_search` couldn't be imported at first, which counted as a single error instead of its two tests.\n\nI made six fixes in `catalog/` and didn't touch any tests:\n\n- **`search.py:3`**: it imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist (`catalog.nonexistent`). It now imports it from `catalog.text`, where the function lives.\n- **`books.py:22`**: `parse_book` kept the year as text (`'1965'`). It now converts it to a number, which also makes `age()` work.\n- **`factory.py`**: added the missing `Emma` (Austen, 1815) to `sample_books()`. Its docstring already said the demo catalog has three titles.\n- **`fees.py:14`**: the late fee added the daily rate to the number of days (`days + 0.25`). It now multiplies them (`days \u00d7 0.25`).\n- **`inventory.py:24`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now returns exactly the last `n`, and an empty list when `n` is 0 or less.\n- **`members.py:4`**: the borrowing limit was set to 3, though the comment above it and the tests both say five. It's now 5.\n\nAs you asked, a subagent investigated the `test_members` failures. It traced both errors to that limit of 3 being lower than the five-book policy.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 53445, "requests_cache_write": 83040, "requests_cost_usd": 0.492657, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 22, "requests_output": 3334, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "n